  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Resonating structure of carbonate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> ion are</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/296d8d16-fa2d-456c-8c26-2b39438519d1-be6ca139-a28a-4b8f-96c4-d250dd3fe4c9-image.png\" style=\"width: 955px; height: 185px;\" /></p><p>In resonating structures bonds are not fixed and therefore, all bond lengths are equal.</p><p>The hybridisation of central atom is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>Thus, there is no coordinate bond present in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>. Hence, the second statement is incorrect.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
